  "market_read": "Baseline run: 16 verified and 1 indicative listing across Pagsanjan and the ~10 km ring. Verified asking prices span PHP 269–3000/sqm with a median of PHP 1200/sqm. The expected Pagsanjan-proper premium is not present — Pagsanjan verified median is PHP 975/sqm against PHP 1600/sqm for the nearby ring. That inversion is composition rather than discount: price per sqm runs inversely to parcel size. The three sub-1-hectare comparables ask PHP 1,200–2,204/sqm, while the ~5 ha blocks that set the median ask PHP 850–1,100/sqm. For a raw 0.5–1 ha Pagsanjan parcel, that points to an asking price of PHP 1,600–1,800/sqm, with PHP 1,400/sqm as the level to price at for the quickest sale. Aging versus cleared inventory is not answerable yet: no source publishes listing dates and there is no prior snapshot to diff against. That signal begins once listings start disappearing between runs."
